# Natural Language to Predicate Logic Converter

![Python Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.8%2B-blue)
![Build Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/tests-passing-brightgreen)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)

## Description

This project provides a robust, modular, two-way translation engine designed to bridge the gap between natural language and formal mathematical logic. Built using Python, it functions as a command-line utility that bidirectionally translates structured English statements into Predicate Logic notations.

In the domain of Artificial Intelligence and Knowledge Representation, converting human-readable facts into machine-parsable logic is a foundational step for automated reasoning and inference systems. This tool implements rule-based parsing algorithms to extract subjects, objects, and quantifiable conditions from strings. 

Specifically, the system identifies standard English quantifiers (such as "all", "every", "some", and "no") and accurately maps them to their respective Universal (∀x) and Existential (∃x) quantifiers in formal logic. Furthermore, it determines the appropriate logical connectors—applying implication (→) for universal statements and conjunction (∧) for existential statements. The reverse engine takes structured predicate expressions, interprets the formal symbols, and reconstructs them into grammatically correct and readable English sentences.

This project was developed to demonstrate practical applications of discrete mathematics and symbolic AI modeling within a clean, test-driven software architecture.

---

## Features

* **English to Predicate Logic:** Detects English quantifiers (*All, some, no, each, etc.*) and maps them to their formal logic counterparts (∀x, ∃x), applying the correct logical connectors (→, ∧).
* **Predicate Logic to English:** Parses complex logic strings and reconstructs readable, grammatically accurate English sentences.
* **Modular Architecture:** Clean separation of concerns across parsing, conversion logic, and utility mappings.
* **Test-Driven:** Includes a comprehensive unit testing suite to validate conversion accuracy in both directions.

